  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 7.85,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare ledger for TRP-02839 have been checked, and the ruling is a PARTIAL_REFUND of S$7.85 to the rider.\n\nThe deviation is established. The governing measurement is the trace (EV-GPS-02839): 24.6 km against the booked optimal of 20.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02839) — an excess of 4.6 km, or 23.0%. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%). It is not a MATERIAL deviation (4.6 km is under the 8.0 km gate and 23.0% is under the 50% gate), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile test is not engaged; in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 197 completed trips in 90 days, far below the 3-flag and 0.05-ratio pattern thresholds, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral arise. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): 193 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gap over 90 seconds and no jump over 500 m.\n\nThe driver's explanation ('KPE closed, LTA advisory on file') does not excuse the excess. The advisory on file is genuine (EV-ADVIS-02839-01: KPE towards ECP after Defu Flyover, 17:53-19:20, shortest lawful alternative 23.0 km), so the assertion is not weightless, but POL-RD-03(c) requires an actual route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after, and the record's own advisory-area test shows the trace never enters the advisory's area — 0 fixes inside it, closest approach 1,350.67 m. The measured excess is not matched to the closure, so POL-RD-03 does not reduce it and the deviation stands at the full 4.6 km measured on the trace. (For completeness: had the closure been accepted, the cap min(4.6, 1.30 x (23.0 - 20.0) + 1.00) = 4.60 km would have left no excess; it does not bite because limb (c) fails.)\n\nThe refund is arithmetic, not discretionary, under POL-RD-02 on the METERED fare. Charged_total 35.01. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 20.0 + 0.28 x 27.0) x 1.00 surge, read from EV-FARE-02839) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 27.16. Refund = 35.01 - 27.16 = 7.85, which is above the S$0.50 de minimis and 22.4% of charged_total, so it is a partial refund and not a full one.\n\nOn the ERP gantry the rider mentions: the trace's closest fix to ECP Fort Rd eastbound is 59.12 m, inside the 250 m crossing radius, so the gantry was in fact crossed. It is a genuine off-route charge, not a phantom line, and POL-RD-09(4) does not fire. Because the deviation is refunded under POL-RD-02, POL-RD-09(1) governs: the S$3.00 off-route ERP is already comprehended in the S$7.85 refund (the recomputed fare carries only on-route gantries) and must never be added on top. The rider's total recovery is S$7.85, not S$10.85.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare ledger, the trace is unimpaired, the refund is far below the S$150.00 ceiling and below charged_total, and the only line without an on-route counterpart (the ERP) is reflected in the POL-RD-02 figure. No clause produces a referral. Profile fields such as rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rate, acceptance rate, active region and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter are context only under POL-GEN-01 and played no part in the outcome; only the counters POL-RD-06 and POL-RD-08 name were used, and neither side meets them. The monetary effect (S$7.85) does not exceed the S$8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
